ainst the first one here  SBC minus  and another issue is that we have all  those separations but they use  artificially constructed formulas  improved complexity people generally  seek to prove separations using  encodings of natural combinatorial  principles because those tend to give  you a more intuitive understanding of  the relative capabilities of the proof  systems so it would be nice to reprove  our results with more natural formulas  also as you might have already inferred  the study of those proof systems kind of  lives on its own Island right now  disconnected from the rest of proof  complexity some things are known for  instance we know that Bond adapt phrase  does not simulate BC minus due to an  existing lower bound  but I think the converse direction is  more interesting for instance is there  any subsystem of frege strictly about  resolution that even a very strong  variant of BC minus simulates  and finally we have a generic recipe in  this work  although it uses some properties quite  specific to the proof systems at hand  could it be maybe possible to somehow  adapt the high level idea for other uses  in proof complexity  and that's it thanks again for listening  also since I gave no explicit references  in the talk here's a list of papers to  look at if you're interested in previous  work
 

